ss=\"mono loc\">shopfast/utils.py</span></td><td class=\"num\">2</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><span class=\"mono\">benchmarks.run_workload</span><br><span class=\"mono loc\">benchmarks/run_workload.py</span></td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">8</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td>entrypoint </td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Entrypoints</h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"mono\">benchmarks.run_workload</span> (benchmarks/run_workload.py): argparse command-line interface, `if __name__ == &#34;__main__&#34;` guard, called from __main__ guard: main</li><li><span class=\"mono\">shopfast.__main__</span> (shopfast/__main__.py): conventional entry file (__main__.py)</li><li><span class=\"mono\">shopfast.api</span> (shopfast/api.py): HTTP route GET /products/{sku}: get_product, HTTP route GET /products/{sku}/polite: get_product_polite, HTTP route GET /rates/{currency}: fetch_exchange_rate</li><li><span class=\"mono\">shopfast.app</span> (shopfast/app.py): argparse command-line interface, `if __name__ == &#34;__main__&#34;` guard, console script &#39;shopfast&#39;, called from __main__ guard: main</li></ul>\n<h3>Import cycles</h3>\n<ul><li class=\"mono\">shopfast.api -&gt; shopfast.app -> shopfast.api</li></ul>\n<h3>Technologies</h3>\n<p><span class=\"tag\">Python <span class=\"muted\">(language)</span></span> <span class=\"tag\">asyncio <span class=\"muted\">(library)</span></span> <span class=\"tag\">SQLite <span class=\"muted\">(database)</span></span> <span class=\"tag\">pytest <span class=\"muted\">(tool)</span></span> </p>\n<h3>Most imported external packages</h3>\n<p><span class=\"tag\">asyncio \u00b7 4</span> <span class=\"tag\">json \u00b7 4</span> <span class=\"tag\">pathlib \u00b7 3</span> <span class=\"tag\">argparse \u00b7 2</span> <span class=\"tag\">collections \u00b7 2</span> <span class=\"tag\">dataclasses \u00b7 2</span> <span class=\"tag\">pytest \u00b7 2</span> <span class=\"tag\">random \u00b7 2</span> <span class=\"tag\">sqlite3 \u00b7 2</span> <span class=\"tag\">time \u00b7 2</span> <span class=\"tag\">copy \u00b7 1</span> <span class=\"tag\">functools \u00b7 1</span> <span class=\"tag\">hashlib \u00b7 1</span> <span class=\"tag\">io \u00b7 1</span> <span class=\"tag\">re \u00b7 1</span> </p>\n<h3>Architecture insights</h3>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> High fan-in module with findings: shopfast.catalog</p>\n  <p>`shopfast.catalog` is imported by 8 modules and has 3 findings. Changes here affect many callers, so fixes have broad reach, but they also need the broadest regression testing; consider giving it focused benchmarks.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Modules: <span class=\"mono\">shopfast.catalog</span> \u00b7 generated by deterministic</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> High fan-in module with findings: shopfast.api</p>\n  <p>`shopfast.api` is imported by 3 modules and has 3 findings. Changes here affect many callers, so fixes have broad reach, but they also need the broadest regression testing; consider giving it focused benchmarks.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Modules: <span class=\"mono\">shopfast.api</span> \u00b7 generated by deterministic</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> High fan-in module with findings: shopfast.orders</p>\n  <p>`shopfast.orders` is imported by 3 modules and has 3 findings. Changes here affect many callers, so fixes have broad reach, but they also need the broadest regression testing; consider giving it focused benchmarks.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Modules: <span class=\"mono\">shopfast.orders</span> \u00b7 generated by deterministic</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Findings outside request paths were deprioritized</p>\n  <p>3 of 24 findings are in code that does not serve requests (CLI_SCRIPT x3). Their priority is scaled down by the path-role factor; review them only if those workflows are slow in practice.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Modules: <span class=\"mono\">shopfast.orders, shopfast.reporting</span> \u00b7 generated by deterministic</p></div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s5\"><span class=\"secnum\">5</span> Prioritized findings</h2>\n<p>24 findings, ordered by priority score (severity, confidence and structural importance). Each finding is a hypothesis about where performance may be lost.</p>\n<table class=\"data findings-table\" repeat=\"1\">\n  <thead><tr><th width=\"5%\">#</th><th width=\"13%\">Severity</th><th width=\"50%\">Finding</th><th width=\"12%\">Confidence</th><th width=\"12%\">Provenance</th><th width=\"8%\" class=\"num\">Priority</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-1\">Nested loops matching items by equality</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:11-12 \u00b7 PP-LOOP-002</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">65.99</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-2\">Database query inside a loop (N+1)</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/orders.py:13-15 \u00b7 PP-DB-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">48.47</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-3\">Database query inside a loop (N+1)</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/orders.py:19-21 \u00b7 PP-DB-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">48.47</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-4\">Re-sorting a growing collection inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/catalog.py:66 \u00b7 PP-LOOP-004</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">41.46</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-5\">Blocking call inside an async function</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/api.py:19 \u00b7 PP-ASYNC-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">40.25</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-6\">List membership test inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/catalog.py:49 \u00b7 PP-LOOP-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">39.61</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-7\">Blocking call inside an async function</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/api.py:31 \u00b7 PP-ASYNC-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">39.00</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-8\">List used as a queue (pop(0)/insert(0, \u2026)) in a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:32 \u00b7 PP-COLL-002</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">32.59</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>9</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-9\">List membership test inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:33 \u00b7 PP-LOOP-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">32.59</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>10</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-10\">List membership test inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:42 \u00b7 PP-LOOP-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">32.09</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>11</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-11\">List membership test inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/catalog.py:41 \u00b7 PP-LOOP-001</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">29.20</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>12</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-12\">String built by repeated concatenation in a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/reporting.py:17 \u00b7 PP-STR-001</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">22.72</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-13\">Linear list search/removal inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:42 \u00b7 PP-COLL-001</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">22.45</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>14</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-14\">Loop-invariant computation repeated every iteration</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/pricing.py:42 \u00b7 PP-LOOP-003</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">22.20</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>15</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-15\">Sequential HTTP request inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/api.py:47 \u00b7 PP-NET-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">20.11</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>16</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-16\">Constant regex pattern processed inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/reporting.py:44 \u00b7 PP-REGEX-001</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">17.75</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>17</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-17\">Overlapping recursion without memoization</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/utils.py:8 \u00b7 PP-CACHE-001</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">17.60</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>18</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-18\">Unbounded module-level cache</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/pricing.py:13 \u00b7 PP-ARCH-002</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">16.14</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>19</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-19\">copy.deepcopy inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/orders.py:52 \u00b7 PP-ALLOC-001</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">14.08</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>20</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-20\">Heavy work at import time</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/reporting.py:8 \u00b7 PP-ARCH-001</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">9.22</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>21</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-21\">Large constant literal rebuilt inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/reporting.py:52-61 \u00b7 PP-ALLOC-002</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">7.68</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>22</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-22\">Constant regex pattern processed inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/reporting.py:31 \u00b7 PP-REGEX-001</span></td><td>LOW</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">7.10</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>23</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-23\">Needless list materialization inside a loop</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/pricing.py:61 \u00b7 PP-COLL-003</span></td><td>HIGH</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">6.98</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>24</td><td><span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span></td><td><a href=\"#f-24\">Same expensive call repeated with identical constant arguments</a><br><span class=\"mono loc\">shopfast/pricing.py:68 \u00b7 PP-CACHE-002</span></td><td>MEDIUM</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td><td class=\"num\">3.66</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-1\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#1 <span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Nested loops matching items by equality</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:11-12</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">reconcile</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-LOOP-002</span> \u00b7 nested loops \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>For every item of `warehouse_rows` (line 10) this code scans all of `catalog` looking for `row[&#39;sku&#39;] == product.sku`. An equality match found by scanning is a join; the number of comparisons is the product of both collection sizes.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Index the inner collection once by the join key, e.g. `by_key = {b.key: b for b in B}` (a dict of lists for non-unique keys), then look up `by_key.get(a.key)` in a single loop.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Join keys must be hashable; duplicate keys need a dict of lists to keep every match; the index costs O(m) memory; result order can differ from the nested-loop order unless you preserve it explicitly.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">reconcile</span> \u2014 825.82 ms cumulative, 822.12 ms internal, 1 calls, 23.8% of profiled time. 23.9% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-2\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#2 <span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Database query inside a loop (N+1)</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/orders.py:13-15</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">order_summaries</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-DB-001</span> \u00b7 database \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>DB-API `execute()` (`cursor.execute(&#39;SELECT id, customer_id, total_cents FROM or\u2026`) runs once per iteration of the loop at line 12. When the loop walks rows or IDs, the number of database round-trips grows with the data (the N+1 query pattern), and each round-trip pays driver and network latency.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Load what the loop needs with one query before it (`WHERE id IN (...)`, `select(...).where(Model.id.in_(ids))`, `selectinload`/`joinedload`, Django `select_related`/`prefetch_related`/`in_bulk`) and look rows up in a dict; batch writes with `executemany`, bulk inserts, or a single UPDATE.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> One large query can return more data and use more memory; IN-lists have database limits (chunk them); batching writes changes transaction and error-reporting granularity; eager loading can over-fetch when only a few rows are used.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">order_summaries</span> \u2014 61.79 ms cumulative, 14.80 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.4% of profiled time. 1.8% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-3\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#3 <span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Database query inside a loop (N+1)</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/orders.py:19-21</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">order_summaries</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-DB-001</span> \u00b7 database \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>DB-API `execute()` (`conn.execute(&#39;SELECT name, tier FROM customers WHERE id = ?\u2026`) runs once per iteration of the loop at line 12. When the loop walks rows or IDs, the number of database round-trips grows with the data (the N+1 query pattern), and each round-trip pays driver and network latency.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Load what the loop needs with one query before it (`WHERE id IN (...)`, `select(...).where(Model.id.in_(ids))`, `selectinload`/`joinedload`, Django `select_related`/`prefetch_related`/`in_bulk`) and look rows up in a dict; batch writes with `executemany`, bulk inserts, or a single UPDATE.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> One large query can return more data and use more memory; IN-lists have database limits (chunk them); batching writes changes transaction and error-reporting granularity; eager loading can over-fetch when only a few rows are used.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">order_summaries</span> \u2014 61.79 ms cumulative, 14.80 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.4% of profiled time. 1.8% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-4\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#4 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Re-sorting a growing collection inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/catalog.py:66</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">top_rated</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-LOOP-004</span> \u00b7 algorithmic \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`best` grows inside the loop at line 64 and is sorted again on every iteration. Each sort is O(k log k) for the current size k, so the total work grows faster than the number of items.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Sort once after the loop, or keep the collection ordered incrementally with `bisect.insort` / a `heapq` priority queue when the order is needed during the loop.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> `heapq` only guarantees the smallest item is first (not a fully sorted list); `bisect.insort` is O(n) per insert because of list shifting but avoids repeated O(n log n) sorts; sort stability and key functions must be preserved.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">top_rated</span> \u2014 80.99 ms cumulative, 10.12 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.3% of profiled time. 2.3% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-5\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#5 <span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Blocking call inside an async function</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/api.py:19</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">get_product</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-ASYNC-001</span> \u00b7 async blocking \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`time.sleep(RATE_LIMIT_SECONDS)` sleeps the whole thread inside `async def get_product`. While it runs, the event loop thread is blocked, so other coroutines (concurrent requests, timers, heartbeats) cannot make progress until it returns.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Use the async equivalent (`await asyncio.sleep`, `httpx.AsyncClient`/`aiohttp`, `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec`, an async DB driver or `AsyncSession`, `aiofiles`), or move the call off the event loop with `await asyncio.to_thread(func, ...)`.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Thread offloading adds thread-pool overhead and requires the code to be thread-safe; async libraries have different APIs, timeouts and exceptions; very short blocking calls (small local files) may not be worth changing.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">get_product</span> \u2014 55.47 ms cumulative, 0.31 ms internal, 20 calls, 0.0% of profiled time. 1.6% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-6\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#6 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List membership test inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/catalog.py:49</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">unique_categories</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-LOOP-001</span> \u00b7 algorithmic \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`product.category not in categories` runs inside a loop and scans `categories`, a list that also grows inside the loop. Membership tests on a list compare elements one by one, so each test costs time proportional to the list length and the loop as a whole can become quadratic as data grows.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Build a set (or dict) once before the loop, e.g. `allowed = set(items)`, and test `x in allowed`; when the list grows inside the loop, maintain a parallel set.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Set elements must be hashable; a set loses ordering and duplicates (keep the list if you need them); building it costs O(m) time and extra memory, so it only pays off when the test runs many times.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">unique_categories</span> \u2014 0.42 ms cumulative, 0.41 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.0% of profiled time. 0.0% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-7\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#7 <span class=\"badge sev sev-high\">HIGH</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Blocking call inside an async function</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/api.py:31</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">fetch_exchange_rate</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-ASYNC-001</span> \u00b7 async blocking \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`urllib.request.urlopen(EXCHANGE_URL.format(currency=currenc\u2026` performs a blocking HTTP request inside `async def fetch_exchange_rate`. While it runs, the event loop thread is blocked, so other coroutines (concurrent requests, timers, heartbeats) cannot make progress until it returns.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Use the async equivalent (`await asyncio.sleep`, `httpx.AsyncClient`/`aiohttp`, `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec`, an async DB driver or `AsyncSession`, `aiofiles`), or move the call off the event loop with `await asyncio.to_thread(func, ...)`.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Thread offloading adds thread-pool overhead and requires the code to be thread-safe; async libraries have different APIs, timeouts and exceptions; very short blocking calls (small local files) may not be worth changing.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-8\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#8 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List used as a queue (pop(0)/insert(0, \u2026)) in a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:32</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">restock_order</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-COLL-002</span> \u00b7 collections \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`queue.pop(0)` removes/inserts at the front of a list inside a loop. Lists are contiguous arrays, so every front operation shifts all remaining elements.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Use `collections.deque` and `popleft()` / `appendleft()`, which are O(1) at both ends.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> A deque does not support slicing and its indexing in the middle is O(n); code that relies on list-only methods (sort, slicing) must change; ordering semantics are the same.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">restock_order</span> \u2014 106.44 ms cumulative, 97.42 ms internal, 1 calls, 2.8% of profiled time. 3.1% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-9\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#9 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List membership test inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:33</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">restock_order</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-LOOP-001</span> \u00b7 algorithmic \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`sku in processed` runs inside a loop and scans `processed`, a list that also grows inside the loop. Membership tests on a list compare elements one by one, so each test costs time proportional to the list length and the loop as a whole can become quadratic as data grows.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Build a set (or dict) once before the loop, e.g. `allowed = set(items)`, and test `x in allowed`; when the list grows inside the loop, maintain a parallel set.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Set elements must be hashable; a set loses ordering and duplicates (keep the list if you need them); building it costs O(m) time and extra memory, so it only pays off when the test runs many times.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">restock_order</span> \u2014 106.44 ms cumulative, 97.42 ms internal, 1 calls, 2.8% of profiled time. 3.1% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-10\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#10 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List membership test inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:42</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">duplicate_skus</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-LOOP-001</span> \u00b7 algorithmic \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`sku not in duplicates` runs inside a loop and scans `duplicates`, a list that also grows inside the loop. Membership tests on a list compare elements one by one, so each test costs time proportional to the list length and the loop as a whole can become quadratic as data grows.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Build a set (or dict) once before the loop, e.g. `allowed = set(items)`, and test `x in allowed`; when the list grows inside the loop, maintain a parallel set.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Set elements must be hashable; a set loses ordering and duplicates (keep the list if you need them); building it costs O(m) time and extra memory, so it only pays off when the test runs many times.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">duplicate_skus</span> \u2014 78.09 ms cumulative, 5.57 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.2% of profiled time. 2.3% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-11\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#11 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List membership test inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/catalog.py:41</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">filter_discontinued</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-LOOP-001</span> \u00b7 algorithmic \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`product.sku not in discontinued_skus` runs inside a loop and scans `discontinued_skus`, which is a list. Membership tests on a list compare elements one by one, so each test costs time proportional to the list length and the loop as a whole can become quadratic as data grows.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Build a set (or dict) once before the loop, e.g. `allowed = set(items)`, and test `x in allowed`; when the list grows inside the loop, maintain a parallel set.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Set elements must be hashable; a set loses ordering and duplicates (keep the list if you need them); building it costs O(m) time and extra memory, so it only pays off when the test runs many times.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">filter_discontinued</span> \u2014 92.19 ms cumulative, 90.00 ms internal, 1 calls, 2.6% of profiled time. 2.7% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-12\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#12 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> String built by repeated concatenation in a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:17</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">render_sales_report</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-STR-001</span> \u00b7 strings \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`report` is extended with `+` on every iteration of the loop at line 16. Python strings are immutable, so each concatenation may allocate a new string and copy everything accumulated so far. CPython can sometimes resize in place (an implementation detail that requires no other references), so the real cost depends on the interpreter and the surrounding code.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Collect the pieces in a list and call `&#39;&#39;.join(parts)` once after the loop, or write them to an `io.StringIO`.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> All pieces stay in memory until the join (similar peak to the final string); output is identical for str; for very few iterations the difference is negligible.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">render_sales_report</span> \u2014 15.71 ms cumulative, 15.71 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.5% of profiled time. 0.5% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-13\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#13 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Linear list search/removal inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:42</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">duplicate_skus</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-COLL-001</span> \u00b7 collections \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`skus.count(sku)` runs inside a loop on a list; `list.count` scans the whole list on every call, so the cost of each call grows with the list length and the loop can become quadratic.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Count all values once with `collections.Counter(items)` and read counts from it.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Values must be hashable; the Counter is a snapshot and must be updated if the list changes; it uses extra memory proportional to the number of distinct values.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">duplicate_skus</span> \u2014 78.09 ms cumulative, 5.57 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.2% of profiled time. 2.3% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-14\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#14 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Loop-invariant computation repeated every iteration</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/pricing.py:42</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">apply_discounts</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-LOOP-003</span> \u00b7 repeated processing \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`sorted(rules, key=lambda r: r.priority)` (copy/sort of a collection) is evaluated on every iteration of the loop at line 41, but none of its inputs change inside that loop, so every iteration after the first repeats identical work.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Compute the value once before the loop and reuse it inside the loop.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Only valid if the inputs really do not change during the loop (including through aliases, other threads, or the file system); hoisting evaluates the expression even when the loop body never runs and moves where exceptions are raised.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">apply_discounts</span> \u2014 78.17 ms cumulative, 26.58 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.8% of profiled time. 1.7% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-15\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#15 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Sequential HTTP request inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/api.py:47</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">fetch_rates</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-NET-001</span> \u00b7 network \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`urllib.request.urlopen(EXCHANGE_URL.format(currency=currenc\u2026` issues an HTTP request on every iteration of the loop at line 46, one after another. Total time grows with the number of iterations multiplied by the request latency.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Use a batch endpoint if the API has one; otherwise issue the requests concurrently with a bound (`asyncio.gather` + `asyncio.Semaphore`, or a `ThreadPoolExecutor` for sync clients), reuse one client/session, and cache repeated responses.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Concurrency increases load on the remote service and can trigger rate limits; error handling, retries and result ordering get more complex; cached responses can be stale.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-16\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#16 <span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Constant regex pattern processed inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:44</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">redact_emails</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-REGEX-001</span> \u00b7 regex \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`re.compile` is called with a constant pattern on every iteration of the loop at line 43. The `re` module caches compiled patterns, so each call is a cache lookup rather than a full compile, but the lookup, argument handling and call overhead repeat for an object that never changes.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Compile the pattern once at module level (`PATTERN = re.compile(...)`) and call `PATTERN.search(...)` (or `.sub`, `.findall`, \u2026) inside the loop.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Module-level compilation runs at import time and keeps the compiled pattern alive for the life of the process; matching behavior is identical.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">redact_emails</span> \u2014 19.99 ms cumulative, 3.53 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.1% of profiled time. 0.6% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-17\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#17 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Overlapping recursion without memoization</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/utils.py:8</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">bundle_combinations</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-CACHE-001</span> \u00b7 caching \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`bundle_combinations` calls itself 2 times per invocation with arguments derived arithmetically from its parameters, and it has no cache. Such tree recursion typically recomputes the same subproblems many times.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Memoize with `@functools.cache` / `@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=...)`, or rewrite the recursion bottom-up/iteratively.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> All arguments must be hashable; the cache keeps every distinct argument tuple and result alive (bound it with maxsize); memoization is only correct for pure functions (same inputs, same output, no side effects); the recursion depth limit still applies.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">bundle_combinations</span> \u2014 158.80 ms cumulative, 158.80 ms internal, 1,028,457 calls, 4.6% of profiled time. 4.6% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-18\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#18 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Unbounded module-level cache</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/pricing.py:13</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-ARCH-002</span> \u00b7 architecture \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`_price_cache` is a module-level dict that functions add entries to, but nothing in this module removes entries or checks its size. If keys come from an unbounded domain (user IDs, request parameters), memory grows for the lifetime of the process.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Bound the cache: `functools.lru_cache(maxsize=...)`, an LRU/TTL cache (for example `cachetools.TTLCache`), or explicit eviction when it exceeds a size.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Eviction causes recomputation on misses; TTL caches can serve stale values until they expire; caches shared between threads need locking or atomic operations.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">&lt;module&gt;</span> \u2014 4.34 ms cumulative, 0.03 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.0% of profiled time. 0.1% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-19\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#19 <span class=\"badge sev sev-medium\">MEDIUM</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> copy.deepcopy inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/orders.py:52</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">history_snapshots</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-ALLOC-001</span> \u00b7 allocations \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`copy.deepcopy(state)` deep-copies the same outer object on every iteration of the loop at line 50. `deepcopy` walks and duplicates the entire object graph (with memo bookkeeping), so each iteration pays for the whole structure, which grows if the loop adds to it.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Copy only what is mutated (a shallow `dict(x)`/`list(x)`/`copy.copy`, `dataclasses.replace`), build new objects instead of mutating copies, or copy once outside the loop if the source does not change.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Shallow copies share nested objects, so mutating nested data would affect the original; only safe after checking which parts are modified.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-20\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#20 <span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Heavy work at import time</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:8</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-ARCH-001</span> \u00b7 architecture \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`open(Path(__file__).with_name(&#39;report_header.txt&#39;), encodin\u2026` opens a file while the module is being imported. Every process that imports this module (web workers, CLI commands, tests) pays this cost and inherits its failure modes before any code path needs the result.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Defer the work until it is needed: move it into a function (optionally cached with `functools.cache`), an application startup hook/lifespan, or a lazily initialized attribute.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Lazy initialization moves the cost and any errors to first use (the first request may be slower); concurrent lazy init needs a lock; some frameworks expect module-level objects.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">&lt;module&gt;</span> \u2014 1.23 ms cumulative, 0.04 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.0% of profiled time. 0.0% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-21\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#21 <span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Large constant literal rebuilt inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:52-61</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">classify_lines</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-ALLOC-002</span> \u00b7 allocations \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>A 8-element constant dict literal is rebuilt on every iteration of the loop at line 51; Python allocates and fills a new container each time even though the contents never change.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Define the literal once outside the loop (a module-level constant; use a tuple or frozenset if it is never modified).</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> A shared constant must not be mutated by the loop body; if it is, keep the per-iteration copy (or copy the constant explicitly).</p></div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-22\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#22 <span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Constant regex pattern processed inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:31</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">extract_skus</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-REGEX-001</span> \u00b7 regex \u00b7 confidence low</p>\n  <p>`re.search` receives a constant pattern on every iteration of the loop at line 30. CPython caches recently compiled patterns (a bounded cache), so this mostly costs a cache lookup per call; it becomes expensive only if many distinct patterns evict each other.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Compile the pattern once at module level (`PATTERN = re.compile(...)`) and call `PATTERN.search(...)` (or `.sub`, `.findall`, \u2026) inside the loop.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Module-level compilation runs at import time and keeps the compiled pattern alive for the life of the process; matching behavior is identical.</p>  <p class=\"measured-evidence\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">e25237f1-6616-4ea6-9902-5effd8a5852d</span>: <span class=\"mono\">extract_skus</span> \u2014 17.64 ms cumulative, 3.82 ms internal, 1 calls, 0.1% of profiled time. 0.5% of profiled time attributed to this function (self time plus direct library calls).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-23\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#23 <span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Needless list materialization inside a loop</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/pricing.py:61</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">region_summary</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-COLL-003</span> \u00b7 allocations \u00b7 confidence high</p>\n  <p>`list(prices_by_region[region].keys())` copies the dict&#39;s keys into a new list on every iteration of the loop at line 60; the temporary list is allocated and discarded each time.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Use the view or iterator directly: `for k in d`, `k in d`, `len(d)`, or `sum(1 for _ in it)` to count an iterator.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Copying `d.keys()` is required when the dict is modified while iterating; consuming an iterator to count it still exhausts it.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card finding\" id=\"f-24\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">#24 <span class=\"badge sev sev-low\">LOW</span> <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Same expensive call repeated with identical constant arguments</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><span class=\"mono\">shopfast/pricing.py:68</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">currency_table</span> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-CACHE-002</span> \u00b7 caching \u00b7 confidence medium</p>\n  <p>`json.loads(RATES_JSON)` is evaluated again with the same constant arguments as on line 67 in `currency_table`; both calls do the same work.</p>\n  <p><strong>Suggestion.</strong> Call it once and reuse the result within the function; if the result is stable across calls, compute it once at module level or cache it with `functools.cache`.</p>\n<p><strong>Trade-offs.</strong> Reusing the result assumes the underlying file, data, or remote resource does not change between the calls; a module-level cache can serve stale data and holds memory.</p></div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s6\"><span class=\"secnum\">6</span> Source references &amp; evidence</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Permalinks are only available for GitHub sources with a known commit SHA.</p>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#1 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Nested loops matching items by equality \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:11-12</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">11</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;matched = []</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">12</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for row in warehouse_rows:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">13</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for product in catalog:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">14</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if row[&#34;sku&#34;] == product.sku:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#2 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Database query inside a loop (N+1) \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/orders.py:13-15</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">13</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;summaries: list[dict[str, object]] = []</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">14</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for order_id in order_ids:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">15</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;cursor.execute(</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">16</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;SELECT id, customer_id, total_cents FROM orders WHERE id = ?&#34;, (order_id,)</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">17</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;)</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#3 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Database query inside a loop (N+1) \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/orders.py:19-21</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">19</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if row is None:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">20</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;continue</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">21</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;customer = conn.execute(</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">22</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;SELECT name, tier FROM customers WHERE id = ?&#34;, (row[1],)</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">23</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;).fetchone()</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#4 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Re-sorting a growing collection inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/catalog.py:66</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">66</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for product in products:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">67</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;best.append(product)</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">68</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;best.sort(key=lambda p: ratings.get(p.sku, 0.0), reverse=True)</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#5 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Blocking call inside an async function \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/api.py:19</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">19</td><td class=\"src\">@router.get(&#34;/products/{sku}&#34;)</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">20</td><td class=\"src\">async def get_product(catalog: list[Product], sku: str) -&gt; Product | None:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">21</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;time.sleep(RATE_LIMIT_SECONDS)</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#6 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List membership test inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/catalog.py:49</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">49</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;categories: list[str] = []</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">50</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for product in products:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">51</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if product.category not in categories:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#7 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Blocking call inside an async function \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/api.py:31</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">31</td><td class=\"src\">@router.get(&#34;/rates/{currency}&#34;)</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">32</td><td class=\"src\">async def fetch_exchange_rate(currency: str) -&gt; float:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">33</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;with urllib.request.urlopen(EXCHANGE_URL.format(currency=currency), timeout=5) as response:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#8 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List used as a queue (pop(0)/insert(0, \u2026)) in a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:32</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">32</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;processed: list[str] = []</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">33</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;while queue:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">34</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;sku = queue.pop(0)</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#9 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List membership test inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:33</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">33</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;while queue:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">34</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;sku = queue.pop(0)</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">35</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if sku in processed:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#10 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List membership test inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:42</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">42</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;duplicates = []</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">43</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for sku in skus:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">44</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if skus.count(sku) &gt; 1 and sku not in duplicates:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#11 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> List membership test inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/catalog.py:41</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">41</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;kept = []</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">42</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for product in products:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">43</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if product.sku not in discontinued_skus:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#12 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> String built by repeated concatenation in a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:17</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">17</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;report = HEADER</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">18</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for order in orders:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">19</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;report += f&#34;{order[&#39;id&#39;]:&gt;6} {order[&#39;customer&#39;]!s:&lt;20} {order[&#39;total_cents&#39;]:&gt;10}\\n&#34;</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#13 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Linear list search/removal inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py:42</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">42</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;duplicates = []</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">43</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for sku in skus:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">44</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if skus.count(sku) &gt; 1 and sku not in duplicates:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#14 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Loop-invariant computation repeated every iteration \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/pricing.py:42</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">42</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;prices = {}</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">43</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for product in products:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">44</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ordered_rules = sorted(rules, key=lambda r: r.priority)</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#15 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Sequential HTTP request inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/api.py:47</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">47</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;rates = {}</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">48</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for currency in currencies:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">49</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;with urllib.request.urlopen(EXCHANGE_URL.format(currency=currency), timeout=5) as response:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#16 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Constant regex pattern processed inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:44</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">44</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;cleaned = []</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">45</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for line in lines:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">46</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;email = re.compile(r&#34;[\\w.+-]+@[\\w-]+\\.[\\w.]+&#34;)</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#17 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Overlapping recursion without memoization \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/utils.py:8</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">8</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">9</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">10</td><td class=\"src\">def bundle_combinations(slots: int) -&gt; int:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#18 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Unbounded module-level cache \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/pricing.py:13</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">13</td><td class=\"src\">RATES_JSON = &#39;{&#34;base&#34;: &#34;USD&#34;, &#34;rates&#34;: {&#34;EUR&#34;: 0.92, &#34;GBP&#34;: 0.79, &#34;KES&#34;: 129.5}, &#34;symbols&#34;: [&#34;EUR&#34;, &#34;GBP&#34;, &#34;KES&#34;]}&#39;</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">14</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">15</td><td class=\"src\">_price_cache = {}</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#19 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> copy.deepcopy inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/orders.py:52</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">52</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for sku, quantity in updates:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">53</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;state[sku] = state.get(sku, 0) + quantity</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">54</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;history.append(copy.deepcopy(state))</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#20 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Heavy work at import time \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:8</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">8</td><td class=\"src\">from pathlib import Path</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">9</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">10</td><td class=\"src\">with open(Path(__file__).with_name(&#34;report_header.txt&#34;), encoding=&#34;utf-8&#34;) as _header_file:</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"evidence\">\n  <p class=\"evidence-head\">#21 <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Large constant literal rebuilt inside a loop \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:52-61</span></p>\n  <table class=\"code\">\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">52</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;scores: dict[str, int] = {}</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">53</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for line in lines:</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">54</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;weights = {</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">55</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;error&#34;: 3,</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">56</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;fail&#34;: 3,</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">57</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;timeout&#34;: 2,</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">58</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;warn&#34;: 2,</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">59</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;slow&#34;: 2,</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">60</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;retry&#34;: 1,</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">61</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;info&#34;: 0,</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln\">62</td><td class=\"src\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#34;ok&#34;: 0,</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"ln