tween threads need locking or atomic operations.</td></tr>    <tr><th>Uncertainty</th><td>Derived from 1 static finding(s) (confidence: MEDIUM x1). Static analysis cannot see input sizes, call frequency or the database/network latency, so the real impact is unknown until the code is profiled before and after the change.</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Findings</th><td class=\"mono\">ae9aeed6eab406ffbce960cf</td></tr><tr><th>Citations</th><td class=\"mono\">shopfast/pricing.py:13</td></tr>    <tr><th>Generated by</th><td>deterministic</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">20. <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> <span class=\"badge effort\">MEDIUM</span> Move heavy work out of import time in shopfast/reporting.py</p>\n  <p>1 heavy work at import time location in module-level code of shopfast/reporting.py. `open(Path(__file__).with_name(&#39;report_header.txt&#39;), encodin\u2026` opens a file while the module is being imported.</p>\n  <table class=\"kv\">\n    <tr><th>Strategy</th><td>Defer the work to a function, a startup hook, or a lazily initialized value.\n- Defer the work until it is needed: move it into a function (optionally cached with `functools.cache`), an application startup hook/lifespan, or a lazily initialized attribute.</td></tr>\n    <tr><th>Rationale</th><td>Static evidence (not measured): `open(Path(__file__).with_name(&#39;report_header.txt&#39;), encodin\u2026` opens a file while the module is being imported. The top location is library code imported by request-handling modules. Execution path: shopfast.api -&gt; shopfast.app -&gt; shopfast.reporting.</td></tr>\n    <tr><th>Expected effect (hypothesis)</th><td>Imports (and therefore startup and test collection) stop paying for it.</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Correctness risks</th><td>Errors surface later (first use instead of import); initialization order changes. Lazy initialization moves the cost and any errors to first use (the first request may be slower); concurrent lazy init needs a lock; some frameworks expect module-level objects.</td></tr>    <tr><th>Uncertainty</th><td>Derived from 1 static finding(s) (confidence: MEDIUM x1). Static analysis cannot see input sizes, call frequency or the database/network latency, so the real impact is unknown until the code is profiled before and after the change.</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Findings</th><td class=\"mono\">dfe8ab6beacaa3d1c85e0d8d</td></tr><tr><th>Citations</th><td class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:8</td></tr>    <tr><th>Generated by</th><td>deterministic</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">21. <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> <span class=\"badge effort\">SMALL</span> Compile constant regular expressions once in extract_skus (shopfast/reporting.py)</p>\n  <p>1 constant regex pattern processed inside a loop location in `extract_skus` (shopfast/reporting.py). `re.search` receives a constant pattern on every iteration of the loop at line 30.</p>\n  <table class=\"kv\">\n    <tr><th>Strategy</th><td>Move constant `re.compile` calls to module level and reuse the compiled pattern.\n- Compile the pattern once at module level (`PATTERN = re.compile(...)`) and call `PATTERN.search(...)` (or `.sub`, `.findall`, \u2026) inside the loop.</td></tr>\n    <tr><th>Rationale</th><td>Static evidence (not measured): `re.search` receives a constant pattern on every iteration of the loop at line 30. The top location is library code imported by request-handling modules. Execution path: shopfast.api -&gt; shopfast.app -&gt; shopfast.reporting:extract_skus.</td></tr>\n    <tr><th>Expected effect (hypothesis)</th><td>Removes per-iteration compilation and cache lookups; the `re` module caches recent patterns, so the effect is usually small.</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Correctness risks</th><td>The module-level constant is created at import time. Module-level compilation runs at import time and keeps the compiled pattern alive for the life of the process; matching behavior is identical.</td></tr>    <tr><th>Uncertainty</th><td>Derived from 1 static finding(s) (confidence: LOW x1). Static analysis cannot see input sizes, call frequency or the database/network latency, so the real impact is unknown until the code is profiled before and after the change.</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Findings</th><td class=\"mono\">63a7b05652385cd10f47f014</td></tr><tr><th>Citations</th><td class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py:31</td></tr>    <tr><th>Generated by</th><td>deterministic</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\">22. <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> <span class=\"badge effort\">SMALL</span> Reuse the result of an expensive call repeated with the same arguments in currency_table (shopfast/pricing.py)</p>\n  <p>1 same expensive call repeated with identical constant arguments location in `currency_table` (shopfast/pricing.py). `json.loads(RATES_JSON)` is evaluated again with the same constant arguments as on line 67 in `currency_table`; both calls do the same work.</p>\n  <table class=\"kv\">\n    <tr><th>Strategy</th><td>Call it once and reuse the result, or cache it when it is stable.\n- Call it once and reuse the result within the function; if the result is stable across calls, compute it once at module level or cache it with `functools.cache`.</td></tr>\n    <tr><th>Rationale</th><td>Static evidence (not measured): `json.loads(RATES_JSON)` is evaluated again with the same constant arguments as on line 67 in `currency_table`; both calls do the same work. The top location is internal code with no known path from an entry point.</td></tr>\n    <tr><th>Expected effect (hypothesis)</th><td>Identical expensive work runs once.</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Correctness risks</th><td>Cached results can go stale if the underlying source changes. Reusing the result assumes the underlying file, data, or remote resource does not change between the calls; a module-level cache can serve stale data and holds memory.</td></tr>    <tr><th>Uncertainty</th><td>Derived from 1 static finding(s) (confidence: MEDIUM x1). Static analysis cannot see input sizes, call frequency or the database/network latency, so the real impact is unknown until the code is profiled before and after the change.</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Findings</th><td class=\"mono\">8ce6cb5487a6ad3f45c8c404</td></tr><tr><th>Citations</th><td class=\"mono\">shopfast/pricing.py:68</td></tr>    <tr><th>Generated by</th><td>deterministic</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s10\"><span class=\"secnum\">10</span> Suggested code changes &amp; diffs</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Diffs are proposals and were never applied to the repository. Patch candidates (listed first, with their lifecycle state) were applied only to isolated copies of the snapshot for correctness validation and A/B benchmarking (sections 11 and 12); a candidate is MEASURED only once it has been validated and benchmarked.</p>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> reconcile (shopfast/inventory_sync.py) \u2014 candidate fb231608 for finding PP-LOOP-002 \u201cNested loops matching items by equality\u201d: COMPLETED, generated by deterministic, finding evidence MEASURED, validation PASSED</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Files: <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/inventory_sync.py</span></p>  <div class=\"diff\">\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">--- a/shopfast/inventory_sync.py</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">+++ b/shopfast/inventory_sync.py</div>\n    <div class=\"dl hunk\">@@ -7,10 +7,12 @@</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;def reconcile(warehouse_rows: list[dict[str, object]], catalog: list[Product]) -&gt; list[tuple[str, int]]:</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;matched = []</div>\n    <div class=\"dl add\">+&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; catalog_by_sku = {}</div>\n    <div class=\"dl add\">+&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; for product in catalog:</div>\n    <div class=\"dl add\">+&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; catalog_by_sku.setdefault(product.sku, []).append(product)</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for row in warehouse_rows:</div>\n    <div class=\"dl del\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; for product in catalog:</div>\n    <div class=\"dl del\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if row[&#34;sku&#34;] == product.sku:</div>\n    <div class=\"dl del\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; matched.append((product.sku, int(str(row[&#34;quantity&#34;]))))</div>\n    <div class=\"dl add\">+&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; for product in catalog_by_sku.get(row[&#34;sku&#34;], ()):</div>\n    <div class=\"dl add\">+&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; matched.append((product.sku, int(str(row[&#34;quantity&#34;]))))</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return matched</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p class=\"card-title\"><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span> Compile constant regular expressions once in redact_emails (shopfast/reporting.py)</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Files: <span class=\"mono\">shopfast/reporting.py</span></p>  <div class=\"diff\">\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">--- a/shopfast/reporting.py</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">+++ b/shopfast/reporting.py</div>\n    <div class=\"dl hunk\">@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;import re</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;from pathlib import Path</div>\n    <div class=\"dl add\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"dl add\">+_REDACT_EMAILS_PATTERN = re.compile(r&#34;[\\w.+-]+@[\\w-]+\\.[\\w.]+&#34;)</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;</div>\n    <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;